From 527da08e498d417ad483b1c00cf2c71c7da4edbc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Fri, 3 Jul 2026 14:26:24 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 05565/11362] [outer-loop] switch planner/retro/audit model to
 codex/gpt-5.5 for quota conservation

Operator: "we are at 31% claude weekly used quota and it is only 50 hours
since the last weekly quota reset. Let's go ahead and switch our planning
and adversarial model entirely over to codex. we want to make sure we have
enough claude code quota headroom for this outer loop and any highly
focused tasks where we know we benefit the most from the superior claude
models."

Changed ~/.config/systemd/user/carnot-conductor.service.d/10-gemini-
routing.conf: AGENT_TYPE_PLANNER/AGENT_TYPE_RETRO claude -> codex,
AGENT_MODEL_PLANNER/AGENT_MODEL_RETRO claude-sonnet-5 -> gpt-5.5. Also set
AGENT_TYPE_AUDIT/AGENT_MODEL_AUDIT (the "adversarial" model -- consumed by
verifier_authenticity_audit.py, pages_adversarial_audit.py, qa_layer_
authenticity_audit.py, arc_self_solve_audit.py) explicitly to codex/gpt-5.5
-- these were previously UNSET here, silently relying on research_
conductor.py's own claude/claude-opus-4-8 defaults.

Retro wasn't named explicitly in the operator's directive ("planning and
adversarial model") but was included: same per-milestone cadence and quota
profile as planner, and leaving it on Claude alone would only partially
serve the stated goal. Flagged for correction if retro was meant to stay.

Verified codex-as-planner has real precedent before flipping (not an
untested path): around milestone .100, AGENT_TYPE_PLANNER=codex was
already used successfully, and the stall-timeout tuning issue from that
era (180s -> 600s for codex) is already in the current code (research_
conductor.py's STALL_TIMEOUT comment).

Applied via systemctl --user daemon-reload && restart; verified via
systemctl --user show -p Environment that all six env vars landed
correctly. The restart interrupted an in-flight experiment task (already
mid-retry after one earlier timeout) -- accepted per the same reasoning as
today's earlier Opus->Sonnet restart, and confirmed the interrupted task's
own pre-authored agent_type: claude override survived the restart
correctly (per-task overrides are independent of the
PLANNER/RETRO/AUDIT-role env vars this change touches).

CLAUDE.md "Codex-Default for Experiments v2" exception #1 updated to
reflect the new routing; ops/known-issues.md documents the directive and
rationale in full.

